@startuml review_layout_03_env_and_mask
' Review unit 03 of 05 -- see docs/review_layout.md for the series.
' State AFTER commit 8b8bfdc (commits 012f99e, 8b8bfdc; docs +52/-74, no code).
' Every case writes the same files as unit 02 (checked at 8b8bfdc).
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/review_layout_03_env_and_mask.puml

title Unit 03 -- run through the conda env; decline the mask layout (14d7be1..8b8bfdc)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
  BorderColor #777777
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  DiamondBorderColor #777777
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #8899AA
  FontColor #33495E
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #C8C08A
}

start

partition ".claude/CLAUDE.md  (012f99e)" {
  #C8E6C9:run Python through the tabray env, an editable install
  a bare python can import a stale installed copy, silently;
  #C8E6C9:conda env create -f environment.yml (the file names it tabray);
  #FFCDD2:"the file names it data_sparsity" -- stale;
  note right
    Shortened during the rebase. The original
    also recorded this machine's two interpreters.
  end note
}

partition "docs/layout_plan.md  (8b8bfdc)" {
  #FFCDD2:mask_fraction, the second parameter of unit 01's plan;
  #C8E6C9:declined: at occupancy 0.149 a mask lands at 0.67-0.92 MB,
  between scattered (1.15 MB) and padded (0.54 MB), so the
  endpoints already bracket it; it would add two parameters and
  a second density denominator, and strand coordinates the
  explainer requires to be used;
  #C8E6C9:recorded so it is not repeated: the real GLORYS land mask on
  a 2000x500 window gave 3.11 MB against 3.31 MB scattered;
  #C8E6C9:text updated for the own-grid density (it said "full-grid");
}

#FFCDD2:<b>dropped</b>: 6875619 "declare scipy" -- main already names the env
tabray and lists pylint; scipy was for the mask, now declined;

:no code change: every case writes the same files as unit 02;

stop

legend right
  |<#C8E6C9> green |= added or changed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFCDD2> red |= removed by THIS unit |
  |<#FFE0B2> orange |= single-variable flow touched by THIS unit |
  |<#FFF9C4> yellow |= generated data or file that changed as a result |
  | plain | unchanged since unit 02 |

  <b>What to review in unit 03</b>
  * the CLAUDE.md rule, and whether more of the
    original machine note is worth keeping
  * the case for declining the mask
end legend

@enduml
